# Project: aussie-park-quiz (React + Vite + Tailwind)

## Goals
- Make minimal, targeted changes.
- Keep the app runnable at all times.
- Preserve existing UI/UX patterns and Tailwind styling.

## Tech Stack & Structure
- Framework: React 18
- Build tool: Vite (ESM)
- Styling: TailwindCSS + PostCSS
- Source layout:
  - src/main.jsx: entry
  - src/App.jsx: main app composition
  - src/components/: UI components
  - src/services/: external API/network logic
  - public/ and signs/: static assets

## Commands
- Dev: `npm run dev`
- Build: `npm run build`
- Preview: `npm run preview`

## Coding Conventions
- Use existing code style in the repository.
- Prefer functional React components and hooks.
- Keep imports at the top of files.
- Use `const` by default; avoid unnecessary reassignments.
- Avoid introducing new dependencies unless necessary.

## Styling Conventions (Tailwind)
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes over new CSS unless there is an existing pattern in `src/index.css`.
- Keep color tokens consistent with `tailwind.config.js` (e.g., `bg-background-light`, `bg-background-dark`).

## API / Secrets
- Never hardcode API keys.
- Poe API key is expected via `import.meta.env.VITE_POE_API_KEY`.
- Do not modify `.env` (it is gitignored). If configuration changes are needed, update `.env.example` only.

## Error Handling
- When adding network calls, handle `response.ok` and surface actionable error messages to the UI.
- Prefer returning structured data from `src/services/*` and keep UI-specific messaging in components.

## Files to Avoid Touching Unless Required
- `package-lock.json` unless dependencies change.
- `dist/` output (should not be committed).
- `.env` (gitignored).

## When Asked To Add Features
- Add or adjust logic in `src/services/*` for API interactions.
- Add UI changes in `src/components/*` and wire in `src/App.jsx`.
- Keep changes small and validate by running `npm run dev` (user-run).
